- [ ] Semantic HTML (`<button>`, `<a>`, `<nav>`, etc.)

**B.4 Performance Review:**
- [ ] LCP < 2.5s (hero image priority / preloaded)
- [ ] Images have width/height to prevent CLS
- [ ] No layout-triggering animations (transform/opacity only)
- [ ] No `window.addEventListener('scroll')` — Motion/ScrollTrigger/IntersectionObserver only
- [ ] Bundle size reasonable (no unnecessary large deps)
- [ ] Lazy loading for below-the-fold content
- [ ] No grain/noise on scrolling containers
- [ ] Google Fonts via `next/font` or `@font-face` with `font-display: swap`
- [ ] Icons from allowed library only
- [ ] Motion isolated in client-leaf components with `'use client'`

**B.5 State & Interaction Review:**
- [ ] Loading state: skeletal loaders matching final layout shape
- [ ] Empty state: composed view with clear "how to populate" guidance
- [ ] Error state: clear inline messages (no `window.alert()`)
- [ ] Button hover states: background shift, scale, or translate
- [ ] Button active/pressed feedback: `scale(0.98)` or `-translate-y-[1px]`
- [ ] Smooth transitions on all interactive elements (200-300ms, not instant)
- [ ] Active nav link styled differently
- [ ] CTA wrap: no label wraps to 2+ lines at desktop
- [ ] No duplicate CTA intent on the page
- [ ] Form: label above input, error below input, no placeholder-as-label

**B.6 Testing Review:**
- [ ] Unit tests for utility functions and hooks
- [ ] Component tests for complex UI components
- [ ] Test coverage for error paths (not just happy path)
- [ ] No commented-out tests left behind
- [ ] Mock setup for external dependencies

**B.7 Full-Output Verification (if multi-file task):**
- [ ] All planned files delivered
- [ ] All planned functions fully implemented
- [ ] No `// ...`, `// TODO`, `/* ... */`, `// implement here` patterns
- [ ] No skeleton when full implementation was requested
- [ ] No "continue later", "you can extend this", "for brevity" patterns

#### E. security-review Post-Review (Security-1 through Security-9)

**Security-1: Authentication & Authorization:**
- [ ] No hardcoded credentials, API keys, or secrets in code
- [ ] Auth tokens have appropriate expiration (access: 15-60min, refresh: 7-30 days)
- [ ] Passwords hashed with bcrypt (cost >= 10) or Argon2
- [ ] Session tokens are random, non-guessable (crypto.randomBytes)
- [ ] Authorization checks on every protected endpoint
- [ ] Ownership/resource-level authorization enforced
- [ ] Privilege escalation prevented (least privilege principle)
- [ ] No authentication bypass in edge cases

**Security-2: Input Validation & Injection:**
- [ ] All user input validated before use
- [ ] SQL injection prevention (parameterized queries, ORM)
- [ ] No string concatenation in SQL, HTML, or shell commands
- [ ] XSS prevention (output encoding, CSP header)
- [ ] Command injection prevention (no exec/eval with user input)
- [ ] Path traversal prevention (canonicalize paths)
- [ ] File upload validation (type, size, content scan)
- [ ] Number/range validation on all numeric inputs
- [ ] Email/URL validation uses established libraries

**Security-3: Data Protection:**
- [ ] Sensitive data not logged (passwords, tokens, PII)
- [ ] Sensitive data encrypted at rest
- [ ] TLS 1.2+ enforced on all external connections
- [ ] Certificate validation enabled (no `verify: false` in production)
- [ ] PII handled per GDPR/compliance requirements
- [ ] Data minimization: only collect/store necessary data
- [ ] API responses do not leak internal details (no stack traces)

**Security-4: API & Webhook Security:**
- [ ] All endpoints require authentication (except intentional public ones)
- [ ] Rate limiting on all endpoints
- [ ] CORS policy correctly configured (not `*` for sensitive APIs)
- [ ] CSRF protection on state-changing operations
- [ ] Webhook signatures verified (HMAC validation)
- [ ] Idempotency enforced on webhook/payment handlers
- [ ] No sensitive data in URLs
- [ ] API versioning in place

**Security-5: LLM / AI Security (ASI Top 10):**
- [ ] Prompt injection: user input sanitized before LLM context
- [ ] No system prompt leakage
- [ ] Output filtering: LLM responses sanitized before display/storage
- [ ] Rate limiting on LLM calls (token budget, request budget)
- [ ] Sensitive data not sent to LLM (PII redaction before context)
- [ ] Tool/function call validation (no unsafe tool execution)
- [ ] Resource exhaustion prevention (max tokens, max steps)
- [ ] Agentic action approval: sensitive actions require human confirmation

**Security-6: Supply Chain & Dependencies:**
- [ ] Lock files committed (`package-lock.json`, `requirements.lock`)
- [ ] Dependency audit run: `npm audit` / `pip check` / `safety check`
- [ ] No `@ts-ignore` masking security warnings
- [ ] No deprecated cryptographic libraries
- [ ] Third-party scripts/CDN resources verified (SRI hashes)
- [ ] License compliance checked for all dependencies

**Security-7: Cryptographic Practices:**
- [ ] No custom cryptographic implementations
- [ ] Strong random number generation (`crypto.getRandomValues`, `secrets.token_bytes`)
- [ ] Keys stored securely (env vars, KMS, vault — not in code)
- [ ] Deprecated algorithms avoided (MD5, SHA1 for hashing, DES, 3DES)
- [ ] IV/nonce is unique per encryption operation
- [ ] JWT signed with RS256/ES256 (not HS256 across services)
- [ ] HTTPS enforced in production (HSTS header)

**Security-8: Error Handling & Logging:**
- [ ] No stack traces or internal paths in error responses
- [ ] User-friendly error messages (no system internals)
- [ ] All security events logged (auth failures, authorization denials)
- [ ] Logs do not contain sensitive data (redacted PII, tokens, passwords)
- [ ] Alerting configured for security anomaly patterns

**Security-9: Advanced RE Review** (if applicable):
- [ ] APK: SSL pinning implemented, no hardcoded secrets in APK
- [ ] Binary: Firmware integrity verified, no hardcoded backdoors
- [ ] JS: No secrets in frontend code, CSP configured, source maps disabled
- [ ] LLM Security: prompt injection defenses, output sanitization

